<section style="font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 980px; margin: 2rem auto; color: #1c1917;">
  <style>
    .slmap-card { border: 1px solid #d6d3d1; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; background: #fafaf9; position: relative; }
    .slmap-card h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .slmap-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 999px; vertical-align: middle; }
    .slmap-items { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; margin-top: 6px; }
    .slmap-item { font-size: 0.7rem; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; background: #e7e5e4; color: #44403c; }
    .slmap-note { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #57534e; margin-top: 6px; line-height: 1.45; }
    .slmap-ordinal { position: absolute; top: -11px; left: 12px; background: #292524; color: #fafaf9; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 1px 9px; border-radius: 999px; }
    .slmap-arrow { text-align: center; color: #a8a29e; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1; margin: 3px 0; }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      section.slmap-root { color: #e7e5e4 !important; }
      .slmap-card { background: #1c1917; border-color: #44403c; }
      .slmap-item { background: #292524; color: #d6d3d1; }
      .slmap-note { color: #a8a29e; }
      .slmap-ordinal { background: #e7e5e4; color: #1c1917; }
    }
  </style>
  <div class="slmap-root">
  <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Slice map — 28 findings → 7 slices, execution order</h3>
  <p class="slmap-note" style="margin-bottom: 1.1rem;">Five independent content slices, then two dependent closers. The shaded band marks the deliberate known-red-goldens window: B1/B2 break snapshot verification until the single sweep-end re-record.</p>

  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px 16px;">

    <div class="slmap-card">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">1</span>
      <h4>core-math <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;">L</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;">independent</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">A1</span><span class="slmap-item">A2</span><span class="slmap-item">A3</span><span class="slmap-item">A4</span><span class="slmap-item">A5</span><span class="slmap-item">A6</span><span class="slmap-item">A7</span><span class="slmap-item">F1</span><span class="slmap-item">F2</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Foundation first. F1/F2 test net lands before the A6 culling change it guards. Breaking: A1 rotation flip (+ documented CCW convention).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">2</span>
      <h4>gesture-coordination <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;">L</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;">independent</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">C1</span><span class="slmap-item">C2</span><span class="slmap-item">C3</span><span class="slmap-item">F4</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Riskiest restructure: one coordinated pointerInput handler subsumes all three findings. Carries the instrumented emulator gate (AC-S3).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">3</span>
      <h4>compose-contracts <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;">M</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;">independent</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">G1</span><span class="slmap-item">E4</span><span class="slmap-item">G3</span><span class="slmap-item">F3</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Group alpha becomes real (additive API + apiDump); annotations and KDoc made honest; alpha test pinned to exact values.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">4</span>
      <h4>view-module <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af;">S</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;">independent</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">D1</span><span class="slmap-item">D2</span><span class="slmap-item">D3</span><span class="slmap-item">G2</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Paint reuse, setter rebuilds, ACTION_UP return, sample KDoc. Small, zero coupling to the Compose work.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card" style="border-color:#f59e0b; background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(245,158,11,0.07), rgba(245,158,11,0.07));">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">5</span>
      <h4>shape-geometry <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af;">S</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;">independent</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;">goldens go red →</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">B1</span><span class="slmap-item">B2</span><span class="slmap-item">B3</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Breaking visual fixes (Octahedron, Knot) sequenced deliberately late: goldens stay red from here until the sweep-end re-record — a two-slice window instead of six.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card" style="border-color:#f59e0b; background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(245,158,11,0.07), rgba(245,158,11,0.07));">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">6</span>
      <h4>docs-and-changelog <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;">M</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fce7f3;color:#9d174d;">← 1, 2, 3, 5</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">E1</span><span class="slmap-item">E2</span><span class="slmap-item">E3</span><span class="slmap-item">G4</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">Docs describe landed behavior: guides, reference tables, CHANGELOG features + per-break migrations, sync-docs.js mirrors. KDoc already traveled with the code.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="slmap-card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1; border-color:#292524; border-width: 2px;">
      <span class="slmap-ordinal">7</span>
      <h4>snapshot-sweep-gate <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af;">S</span> <span class="slmap-badge" style="background:#fce7f3;color:#9d174d;">← all six</span></h4>
      <div class="slmap-items"><span class="slmap-item">AC-S1 test+apiCheck</span><span class="slmap-item">AC-S2 golden re-record + attribution</span><span class="slmap-item">AC-S3 evidence checkpoint</span><span class="slmap-item">doc screenshots</span></div>
      <p class="slmap-note">One deliberate re-record; every changed PNG attributed to a named fix (B1, B2, maybe G1) — an unattributable diff reopens its owning slice. Gate closes on <em>CI</em> green, not local green (Windows→Linux pixel-drift caveat).</p>
    </div>

  </div>
  </div>
</section>
